# Webhook Reliability Rules

- Sign every webhook body with direction-specific merchant secret.
- Include event metadata (`method`, `timestamp`, payload identifiers) in a stable schema.
- Retry delivery on non-200 responses with bounded attempts and backoff.
- Treat webhook processing as at-least-once: design handlers to be idempotent.
- Do not assume delivery order; state should be derived from explicit status value.
- Persist delivery attempts with request body hash, response code, attempt number, and timestamp.
- Expose safe re-delivery tooling from admin/merchant UI where supported.
